	"notes": "This is a blog index with 212 posts. At the top there is a welcome banner (a title and a 3D picture of skis) whose margins are a percentage of the screen, so it really does stretch wider on a bigger monitor. But scroll past it — visible only in our full-page shot — and the actual list of posts is a row of three equal cards that stops growing at 1280 pixels no matter how wide the screen gets; a desktop and an ultrawide monitor show the exact same size grid; you just get more empty space on the sides. On a phone both parts collapse to a single column and the picture moves above the words instead of beside them. It is a small but real example of the same page mixing a growing, fluid section with a capped, centred one, which is exactly the kind of thing a screenshot alone hides and only measuring the boxes reveals.",
